# Schema selectors and configuration forms

A selector tells a form what kind of value to accept and how Home Assistant helps someone supply it. Keep the value type, filters and validation that Home Assistant supplies. A selector does not grant permission and does not show that a target is available now.

<h2 id="selection">Choose resources, providers and destinations</h2>

Entity, device, area, floor, label and target selectors use stable identities and native filters. See [Entity, device and area pickers](target-pickers.html#ha-ctrl-008-capabilities). Config entry, app, backup location, serial port and provider selectors point at different kinds of resource. Do not flatten them into a list of entity IDs. An attribute depends on its parent entity. A statistic has its own identity and may have no current state entity.

Assist pipeline, conversation agent, speech-to-text, text-to-speech and voice choices keep their provider links and permissions. A provider can be a cloud service. Say so only where the actual configuration shows it. Language, country and time zone are separate preferences. Changing the language must not silently change units or the household time zone.

